        "id": 1000187
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-08-18T21:47:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, but doing enable_interrupt(0) then enable_interrupt(1) does make extra interrupts happen.\n\nAnd just leaving the interrupt enabled causes interrupt storms.\n\nSo I\u0027ll only enable it during debouncing, the same as the other state machines.  If Cr50 is in deep sleep, it will be necessary to toggle AC detect to wake it up, at which point it\u0027ll detect cable insertion.\n\nThat\u0027s necessary on Eve anyway, because if Cr50 is in deep sleep and EC is hibernating, Cr50 thinks the cable is attached already and won\u0027t trigger on an actual insert.",
      "parentUuid": "f962fd81_4a0262b9",
